# Page snapshots

Before changing selectors, open `snapshots/INDEX.md`, then the page’s `outline.txt` (tree) and `.html` (full slimmed markup), plus site CSS in `snapshots/css/`.

- Match `@-moz-document` in `style.config.mjs` to the page you are styling (`src/base.scss` is global; `src/pages/*` is per-page).
- Prefer class and id selectors. Keep `:nth-child` only for unique chrome that has no class/id (header/nav is never collapsed in snapshots).
- Treat `<!-- snapshot: omitted … -->` as a gap: sibling counts after that comment are not the live page’s `:nth-child` indices.
- Recapture a page with Alt+Shift+S (dev userscript) after Gelbooru markup changes, or run `npm run snapshot:fetch` for public pages.
- Selector hover previews come from the same live capture (`snapshots/previews/`). Run `npm run preview:install` once, reload the window, then hover a selector in `src/**/*.scss`.
